---
import "../styles/global.css";

const canonicalURL = new URL(Astro.url.pathname, Astro.site);
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Engrams is the Schema Runtime for AI agents. It isn't a passive memory store or static markdown rules — it's an active runtime that finds, defines, and refines mental models like the human brain."
    />
    <link rel="canonical" href={canonicalURL} />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <title>Engrams — The Schema Runtime for AI Agents</title>
  </head>
  <body class="runtime-body">
    <!-- ── TOP BAR ── -->
    <header class="top-bar">
      <div class="bar-inner">
        <a href="/" class="brand">
          <span class="glyph">⬡</span>
          <span class="name">ENGRAMS</span>
          <span class="version">v0.14.0</span>
        </a>
        <nav class="nav">
          <a href="#what">What is a Schema</a>
          <a href="#runtime">Why a Runtime</a>
          <a href="#lifecycle">How It Learns</a>
          <a href="/docs/guide/cognitive-schemas" class="highlight">Guide</a>
          <a href="/docs/getting-started">Docs</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/stevebrownlee/engrams-cli" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub ↗</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main class="page-content">
      <!-- ══ 1. THE HERO ══ -->
      <section class="hero-section">
        <h1 class="hero-title">
          The Schema Runtime<br />
          <span class="accent">for AI Coding Agents.</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="hero-lede">
          Static markdown rules bloat your prompt. Flat memory stores sit passively waiting to be queried.
          Engrams is an <strong>active runtime</strong> that continuously finds, defines, and refines
          mental models for your codebase — just like the human brain.
        </p>

        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a href="/docs/quick-start" class="btn-action primary">5-Minute Quick Start</a>
          <a href="/docs/guide/cognitive-schemas" class="btn-action secondary">Read the Schema Guide</a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ══ 2. WHY A RUNTIME? (CATEGORICAL SEPARATION) ══ -->
      <section id="runtime" class="content-section">
        <h2 class="section-heading">Why a Schema Runtime?</h2>
        <p class="section-description">
          Other tools treat AI context as static files or dead databases. A runtime is different:
          it actively perceives changes, clusters patterns, and executes directives at the exact point of action.
        </p>

        <div class="runtime-matrix">
          <div class="matrix-card">
            <span class="matrix-tag tag-muted">PASSIVE MEMORY STORES</span>
            <h3>Vector Databases &amp; ADR Lists</h3>
            <div class="matrix-flaw">Dead history waiting to be searched</div>
            <p>
              Stores hundreds of isolated notes. But the agent has no trigger condition — it doesn't know
              <em>when</em> a rule applies. It either queries blindly or ignores your history completely.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="matrix-card">
            <span class="matrix-tag tag-muted">STATIC RULES FILES</span>
            <h3>Prompt Stuffing &amp; <code>.cursorrules</code></h3>
            <div class="matrix-flaw">Brittle, manual, and bloated</div>
            <p>
              Developers manually write rigid text rules that get dumped into every prompt regardless of relevance.
              Consumes context window space and causes severe attention decay in reasoning models.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="matrix-card matrix-featured">
            <span class="matrix-tag tag-teal">THE ENGRAMS RUNTIME</span>
            <h3>Active Cognitive Schemas</h3>
            <div class="matrix-flaw text-teal">Continuous perception &amp; 1ms execution</div>
            <p>
              Autonomously clusters codebase activity, formalizes triggers and directives, and intercepts agent
              edits in 1ms with compact 250-token playbooks.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ══ 3. WHAT IS A SCHEMA? ══ -->
      <section id="what" class="content-section">
        <h2 class="section-heading">What is a Schema?</h2>
        <p class="section-description">
          Human experts don't re-read the company manual before every task. They rely on <strong>cognitive schemas</strong>:
          intuitive mental models that sleep until a specific context wakes them up.
          Engrams formalizes this into three machine-executable elements:
        </p>

        <div class="specimen-card">
          <div class="sc-header">
            <div class="sc-title">
              <span class="sc-badge">SCHEMA</span>
              <code>payment-adapters</code>
            </div>
            <span class="sc-status">● active runtime concept · 1ms SQLite</span>
          </div>

          <div class="sc-content">
            <div class="sc-row">
              <span class="sc-k">⚡ TRIGGER</span>
              <div class="sc-v">
                <strong>When does this concept activate?</strong>
                <p>Fires when editing payment adapter implementations under <code>src/adapters/</code></p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="sc-row">
              <span class="sc-k">📋 DIRECTIVE</span>
              <div class="sc-v">
                <strong>What operational rule must be executed?</strong>
                <p class="rule-box">
                  Implement PaymentProvider trait; pass idempotency_key to all charge requests; verify signatures with crypto::constant_time_eq; never log raw payload tokens.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="sc-row">
              <span class="sc-k">🔗 MEMBERS</span>
              <div class="sc-v">
                <strong>What decisions and code anchors prove why?</strong>
                <div class="sc-members">
                  <span class="m-pill">ADR #44: PaymentProvider interface contract</span>
                  <span class="m-pill">Pattern #8: Constant-time signature verification</span>
                  <span class="m-pill anchor">Anchor: src/adapters/stripe.rs</span>
                  <span class="m-pill anchor">Anchor: src/billing/service.rs</span>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="anatomy-grid">
          <div class="anatomy-item">
            <h3>1. The Activation Trigger</h3>
            <p>
              The precise operational scope. Schemas don't float in global context; they sleep until matching file paths
              or task tags wake them up.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="anatomy-item">
            <h3>2. The Operational Directive</h3>
            <p>
              The non-negotiable invariant the AI must follow. Not passive history, but an actionable directive that
              prevents bugs and convention drift upfront.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="anatomy-item">
            <h3>3. Bundled Knowledge Members</h3>
            <p>
              The underlying ADRs, patterns, and code anchors that ground the rule. If the AI needs to verify <em>why</em>,
              the contracts and reasoning are already attached.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ══ 4. HOW THE RUNTIME LEARNS: FINDS, DEFINES, REFINES, EXECUTES ══ -->
      <section id="lifecycle" class="content-section">
        <h2 class="section-heading">How the Runtime Learns</h2>
        <p class="section-description">
          The human brain doesn't require manual file editing to form intuition. Engrams runs a continuous
          cognitive loop: perceiving clusters, defining boundaries, adapting to drift, and executing just in time.
        </p>

        <div class="loop-grid">
          <!-- Step 1: Finds -->
          <div class="loop-card">
            <div class="lc-stage">01 / PERCEPTION</div>
            <h3>Finds</h3>
            <p>
              As you commit code and log decisions, graph community detection identifies natural clusters
              of co-edited files and decisions in local SQLite.
            </p>
            <pre class="lc-code"><code>$ engrams schema scan</code></pre>
          </div>

          <!-- Step 2: Defines -->
          <div class="loop-card">
            <div class="lc-stage">02 / ACCOMMODATION</div>
            <h3>Defines</h3>
            <p>
              At session close, Engrams nudges you with ready-to-run confirm commands, and authoring enforces
              strict trigger-and-rule contracts.
            </p>
            <pre class="lc-code"><code>$ engrams schema confirm decision:10 \
    --name payment-adapters</code></pre>
          </div>

          <!-- Step 3: Refines -->
          <div class="loop-card">
            <div class="lc-stage">03 / ADAPTATION</div>
            <h3>Refines</h3>
            <p>
              Tracks git staleness drift, records retrieval surface counts, and re-notifies when new candidate
              evidence advances beyond prior notifications.
            </p>
            <pre class="lc-code"><code>$ engrams schema refine payment-adapters \
    --trigger "..." --rule "..."</code></pre>
          </div>

          <!-- Step 4: Executes -->
          <div class="loop-card lc-featured">
            <div class="lc-stage text-orange">04 / ACTION</div>
            <h3>Executes</h3>
            <p>
              Tomorrow, your AI touches matching files. <code>engrams advise</code> intercepts the edit in 1ms,
              injecting the active schema before a single line is written.
            </p>
            <pre class="lc-code"><code>$ engrams advise src/adapters/stripe.rs</code></pre>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ══ 5. THREE COMMANDS THAT RUN IT ══ -->
      <section class="content-section">
        <h2 class="section-heading">Three Operational Levers</h2>
        <p class="section-description">
          Your AI executes the advice automatically. You steer the runtime with three high-leverage commands.
        </p>

        <div class="cmd-stack">
          <div class="cmd-box">
            <div class="cb-chrome">
              <span class="cb-cmd">$ engrams advise src/adapters/stripe.rs</span>
              <span class="cb-desc">RUNTIME PRE-EDIT INTERCEPTOR</span>
            </div>
            <pre class="cb-body"><code>&#123;
  "schemas": [
    &#123;"id": 1, "name": "payment-adapters", "summary": "Fires when editing payment adapters: implement PaymentProvider..."&#125;
  ],
  "constraints": [ ... ]
&#125;</code></pre>
          </div>

          <div class="cmd-box">
            <div class="cb-chrome">
              <span class="cb-cmd">$ engrams schema show payment-adapters</span>
              <span class="cb-desc">CONCEPTUAL INSPECTION CONSOLE</span>
            </div>
            <pre class="cb-body"><code>&#123;
  "name": "payment-adapters",
  "summary": "Fires when editing payment adapters...",
  "guided": 14,
  "members": [ ... ]
&#125;</code></pre>
          </div>

          <div class="cmd-box">
            <div class="cb-chrome">
              <span class="cb-cmd">$ engrams session close --pr 42</span>
              <span class="cb-desc">OPPORTUNITY NUDGE &amp; TOKEN RECEIPT</span>
            </div>
            <pre class="cb-body"><code>&#123;
  "schema_value": &#123;"guided_retrievals": 6, "distinct_schemas": 2&#125;,
  "schema_opportunities": [
    &#123;"confirm_command": "engrams schema confirm decision:10 --name auth-rules"&#125;
  ]
&#125;</code></pre>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ══ 6. INSTALL ══ -->
      <section class="install-section">
        <div class="install-box">
          <h2>Give your AI the mental models it deserves.</h2>
          <p>Local SQLite engine. 0MB background memory. 1ms query execution.</p>
          <div class="install-code">
            <code>cargo install engrams-cli</code>
            <span class="sep">or</span>
            <code>brew install stevebrownlee/tap/engrams</code>
          </div>
          <div class="install-actions">
            <a href="/docs/quick-start" class="btn-action primary">5-Minute Quick Start</a>
            <a href="/docs/guide/cognitive-schemas" class="btn-action secondary">Read the Full Guide</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <!-- ── FOOTER ── -->
    <footer class="bottom-footer">
      <div class="footer-wrap">
        <span class="footer-brand">⬡ ENGRAMS · Apache-2.0 · The Schema Runtime for AI Agents</span>
        <div class="footer-links">
          <a href="/docs/guide/cognitive-schemas">Cognitive Schemas</a>
          <a href="/docs/getting-started">Docs</a>
          <a href="/docs/reference/cli">CLI Reference</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/stevebrownlee/engrams-cli" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  /* ============================================================
     COOLORS PALETTE: #ff9f1c | #ffbf69 | #ffffff | #cbf3f0 | #2ec4b6
     Text: Deep Pine (#0c2423) for crisp, authoritative contrast
     Zero black background. Zero tiny headers above large headers.
     ============================================================ */

  :root {
    --c-orange:       #ff9f1c; /* primary warm action */
    --c-peach:        #ffbf69; /* soft warm secondary */
    --c-white:        #ffffff; /* crisp white */
    --c-aqua:         #cbf3f0; /* ice aqua / border / tint */
    --c-teal:         #2ec4b6; /* vibrant teal / brand */
    --c-pine:         #0c2423; /* high-contrast dark text */
    --c-pine-muted:   #345351; /* secondary text */
    --c-surface:      #ffffff;
    --c-surface-subtle: #f5fcfa;
    --c-border:       #cbf3f0;
    --c-border-strong: #2ec4b6;
    --font-mono: 'SFMono-Regular', Consolas, 'Liberation Mono', Menlo, monospace;
    --font-sans: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
  }

  .runtime-body {
    background: var(--c-white);
    color: var(--c-pine);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
  }

  /* ── TOP BAR ── */
  .top-bar {
    position: fixed;
    top: 0; left: 0; right: 0;
    z-index: 100;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.95);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--c-border);
    backdrop-filter: blur(8px);
  }
  .bar-inner {
    max-width: 72rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0.85rem 1.5rem;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .brand { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 0.4rem; text-decoration: none; color: var(--c-pine); }
  .glyph { color: var(--c-orange); font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 900; }
  .name { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-weight: 900; font-size: 1.05rem; letter-spacing: 0.05em; color: var(--c-pine); }
  .version { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.72rem; color: var(--c-teal); margin-left: 0.2rem; font-weight: 700; }
  .nav { display: flex; gap: 1.4rem; }
  .nav a { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.82rem; color: var(--c-pine-muted); text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600; transition: color 0.15s; }
  .nav a:hover { color: var(--c-teal); }
  .nav a.highlight { color: var(--c-orange); font-weight: 800; }
  @media (max-width: 760px) { .nav a:not(:last-child):not(.highlight) { display: none; } }

  /* ── MAIN CONTENT CONTAINER ── */
  .page-content {
    max-width: 72rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 7rem 1.5rem 4rem;
  }

  /* ── 1. HERO ── */
  .hero-section {
    margin-bottom: 5.5rem;
    text-align: left;
    padding: 2.5rem 0 1rem;
  }
  .hero-title {
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5.8vw, 4.4rem);
    font-weight: 900;
    line-height: 1.08;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    color: var(--c-pine);
    margin: 0 0 1.6rem;
  }
  .hero-title .accent {
    color: var(--c-teal);
    display: block;
  }
  .hero-lede {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--c-pine-muted);
    max-width: 52rem;
    margin-bottom: 2.4rem;
  }
  .hero-lede strong { color: var(--c-pine); }
  .hero-actions { display: flex; gap: 1rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }

  /* ── TECHNICAL BUTTONS (SHARP RECTANGULAR, ZERO PILLS) ── */
  .btn-action {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 0.8rem 1.6rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-decoration: none;
    border-radius: 2px;
    border: 2px solid transparent;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: all 0.15s;
  }
  .btn-action.primary {
    background: var(--c-orange);
    color: #ffffff;
    border-color: var(--c-orange);
  }
  .btn-action.primary:hover {
    background: #e68e17;
    border-color: #e68e17;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 14px rgba(255, 159, 28, 0.35);
  }
  .btn-action.secondary {
    background: var(--c-white);
    color: var(--c-teal);
    border-color: var(--c-teal);
  }
  .btn-action.secondary:hover {
    background: var(--c-aqua);
    color: #1b8a80;
  }

  /* ── COMMON SECTION HEADERS (NO TINY LABELS) ── */
  .content-section {
    margin-bottom: 6rem;
    padding-top: 3.5rem;
    border-top: 2px solid var(--c-aqua);
  }
  .section-heading {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    font-weight: 900;
    color: var(--c-pine);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    line-height: 1.15;
  }
  .section-description {
    font-size: 1.18rem;
    color: var(--c-pine-muted);
    line-height: 1.65;
    max-width: 52rem;
    margin-bottom: 2.8rem;
  }
  .section-description strong { color: var(--c-pine); }

  /* ── 2. RUNTIME MATRIX (THREE-WAY SPLIT) ── */
  .runtime-matrix {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }
  .matrix-card {
    background: var(--c-surface-subtle);
    border: 1px solid var(--c-border);
    padding: 2rem 1.8rem;
    border-radius: 2px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }
  .matrix-featured {
    border: 2px solid var(--c-teal);
    background: #ffffff;
    box-shadow: 0 8px 30px rgba(46, 196, 182, 0.12);
  }
  .matrix-tag {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    margin-bottom: 0.8rem;
  }
  .tag-muted { color: var(--c-pine-muted); }
  .tag-teal { color: var(--c-teal); }
  .matrix-card h3 {
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--c-pine);
    margin: 0 0 0.4rem;
  }
  .matrix-flaw {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--c-pine-muted);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .text-teal { color: var(--c-teal); }
  .text-orange { color: var(--c-orange); }
  .matrix-card p {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--c-pine-muted);
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .matrix-card strong { color: var(--c-pine); }

  /* ── 3. WHAT IS A SCHEMA (SPECIMEN CARD) ── */
  .specimen-card {
    background: var(--c-white);
    border: 2px solid var(--c-border);
    border-radius: 2px;
    margin-bottom: 2.8rem;
    box-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgba(12, 36, 35, 0.06);
  }
  .sc-header {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 1rem 1.5rem;
    background: var(--c-surface-subtle);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--c-border);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }
  .sc-title { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.6rem; }
  .sc-badge {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    background: var(--c-orange);
    color: #ffffff;
    padding: 0.15rem 0.5rem;
    border-radius: 2px;
  }
  .sc-title code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--c-pine);
  }
  .sc-status {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--c-teal);
    font-weight: 800;
  }
  .sc-content { padding: 2rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1.5rem; }
  .sc-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 130px 1fr; gap: 1.25rem; align-items: baseline; }
  @media (max-width: 680px) { .sc-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0.4rem; } }
  .sc-k {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--c-teal);
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }
  .sc-v strong { display: block; font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--c-pine-muted); margin-bottom: 0.25rem; font-family: var(--font-mono); }
  .sc-v p { margin: 0; font-size: 1.02rem; color: var(--c-pine); line-height: 1.6; }
  .sc-v code { font-family: var(--font-mono); color: var(--c-teal); font-size: 0.9em; background: #e8f8f6; padding: 0.1rem 0.35rem; border-radius: 2px; }
  .rule-box {
    font-family: var(--font-mono) !important;
    font-size: 0.94rem !important;
    background: #fdf6ec;
    border: 1px solid #ffd8a8;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--c-orange);
    padding: 0.9rem 1.2rem;
    border-radius: 2px;
    color: #7a4100 !important;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .sc-members { display: flex; gap: 0.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 0.4rem; }
  .m-pill {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    padding: 0.35rem 0.75rem;
    background: var(--c-surface-subtle);
    border: 1px solid var(--c-border);
    color: var(--c-pine-muted);
    border-radius: 2px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .m-pill.anchor { color: #15796f; border-color: var(--c-teal); background: #eaf8f7; }

  .anatomy-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }
  .anatomy-item {
    background: var(--c-surface-subtle);
    border: 1px solid var(--c-border);
    padding: 1.8rem;
    border-radius: 2px;
  }
  .anatomy-item h3 { font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 800; color: var(--c-pine); margin: 0 0 0.5rem; }
  .anatomy-item p { font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--c-pine-muted); line-height: 1.6; margin: 0; }

  /* ── 4. HOW IT LEARNS (LOOP GRID) ── */
  .loop-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr));
    gap: 1.25rem;
  }
  .loop-card {
    background: var(--c-white);
    border: 1px solid var(--c-border);
    border-radius: 2px;
    padding: 1.8rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: space-between;
  }
  .lc-featured {
    border: 2px solid var(--c-teal);
    background: #f7fdfc;
  }
  .lc-stage {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
